-- title:
--   Frobenius-fixed divisor classes counted by the class number
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a finite field, $K$ an algebraically closed field, and $F_0$, $F$ fields with $F_0$ a $k$-algebra, $F$ a $K$-algebra and $F$ an $F_0$-algebra; assume `IsCurveOver k F₀` and `IsCurveOver K F`, that is: for each field every nonzero element has an associated divisor of degree zero recording its orders at all places, every place has residue field finite over the constant field, and the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank one over the function field. Assume further that $F_0$ is generated over $k$, as an intermediate field, by a finite set; that `ConstantsAreBase k F₀` holds, i.e. the Riemann–Roch space of the zero divisor of $F_0/k$ is exactly the image of $k$; that the intermediate field of $F/K$ generated by the image of $F_0$ is all of $F$; and that, with $q = \operatorname{card} k$, every $a \in K$ satisfies $a^{q^n} = a$ for some $n > 0$ (no $k$-algebra structure on $K$ is assumed). Let $\varphi \colon F \to F$ be a $K$-algebra endomorphism whose underlying ring homomorphism is integral and which acts on the image of $F_0$ by $x \mapsto x^{q}$, and let $T$ be an additive endomorphism of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(F/K)$ — the group of degree-zero divisors modulo principal ones — that sends the class of each degree-zero divisor $D$ to the class of its push-forward `Divisor.pushforwardAlong φ hφi D` (on places, inertia degree times restriction along $\varphi$). Then the set of fixed points of $T$ is finite, and its cardinality equals $\operatorname{card} \mathrm{Pic}^0(F_0/k)$.
--
--   This is F. K. Schmidt's descent statement for divisor classes over a finite field, in the form counting the points of the Jacobian of $F/K$ fixed by the Frobenius push-forward: they are exactly the classes coming from $F_0/k$, so their number is the class number $h$ of $F_0/k$. It feeds the computation of the characteristic polynomial of Frobenius on divisor classes in [`AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.exists_monic_natCard_fixedPoints_iterate_eq_resultant_of_pushforwardAlong_frobenius`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.exists_monic_natCard_fixedPoints_iterate_eq_resultant_of_pushforwardAlong_frobenius), and thence the rationality and functional equation of the zeta function of a curve over a finite field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Pic0_natCard_fixedPoints_eq_natCard_pic0_of_pushforwardAlong_frobenius.lean

